# ─── Sapt configuration ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your values.

# REQUIRED — your Sapt project UUID (from the Sapt dashboard).
# Powers analytics and the booking funnel (POST → CRM). To save bookings you
# also create the `booking` CRM type once — see SAPT_SETUP_GUIDE.md, section 4.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SAPT_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id-here

# OPTIONAL — API base URL (defaults to https://api.sapt.ai).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SAPT_BASE_URL=https://api.sapt.ai

# OPTIONAL — the shop's Meta Pixel id (digits only, from Events Manager).
# Unset, no Meta code loads at all. Set, every page sends a PageView and each
# booking sends a Lead that Sapt's server-side copy dedupes against; connect
# the same pixel under Sapt's Meta conversions so both halves count once.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=

# OPTIONAL — analytics ingest URL (defaults to https://ingest.sapt.ai).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SAPT_INGEST_URL=https://ingest.sapt.ai

# OPTIONAL (SERVER-ONLY SECRET) — what `pnpm pull-gbp` authenticates with to
# read the client's Google Business Profile through Sapt. The site itself never
# uses it: CMS content comes from Sapt's public read.
# Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never commit a real key.
# SAPT_API_KEY=sapt_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# OPTIONAL (SERVER-ONLY SECRET) — the key Sapt signs its content webhook with.
# With it, /api/revalidate rebuilds pages the moment content is published;
# without it, edits show on a timer. In production set it with
# `pnpm wrangler secret put APP_KEY`. See SAPT_SETUP_GUIDE.md, section 5.
# APP_KEY=

# OPTIONAL (SERVER) — which Google Business Profile location `pnpm pull-gbp`
# reads. Only needed when the Sapt project has more than one; otherwise it uses
# the only one there is. The script prints the available ids when it cannot
# pick.
# GBP_LOCATION_ID=

# OPTIONAL (SERVER) — CRM typed-record slug for bookings (defaults to "booking").
# SAPT_BOOKING_TYPE_SLUG=booking
